1790372066059142	bones-yzou15	itc:v3:AWLJPM5OcyTJJJEAAAAAQdXt13atVUAAAAEzEQ		item.comment	bn-t694	{"body":"Severity (from bn-24t4): LATENT for users. apply_event assigns fields (item_state.rs:235-460) instead of merging, and the SQLite projection ignores LWW entirely. LwwRegister::compare only matters for WorkItemState::merge and compaction. Still fix it: Merge claims semilattice laws, and the projection fix may start to use it. Real divergence bug filed separately."}	blake3:XJjHCV4F5EQtqejG0gKGZw281sEHERexj3O8HXrDgrw
1790372066190651	bones-yzou15	itc:v3:AWLJPM5OcyTJJJEAAAAAQdXt13atVUAAAAEzEg		item.create	bn-1ugh	{"description":"Found by bn-24t4. Verified: git check-attr gives merge=union for .bones/events/*.events, and db/project.rs uses plain UPDATEs.\n\nCause:\n- The SQLite projection (db/project.rs:420-465 fields, :526-535 state) does 'UPDATE items SET <field> = ?' per event. It checks no wall_ts, ITC or hash. The last event applied wins.\n- rebuild streams shards in filename order, then line order (rebuild.rs:227, shard.rs:621). No sort.\n- .bones/.gitattributes sets 'events/*.events merge=union' (written by bones-core lib.rs:41). This deeper file overrides the root '*.events merge=bones-events' entry that bn sync writes (cmd/sync.rs:102). So the sorting merge driver (sync/merge.rs:107, sorts by wall_ts, agent, hash) never runs.\n- Union merge puts 'ours' lines first, then 'theirs'.\n\nScenario (no clock skew needed):\n- A and B start at base S. A appends 'update title=X'. B appends 'update title=Y'.\n- Each does a plain 'git pull' (merge). A's file: [S, X, Y], title=Y. B's file: [S, Y, X], title=X.\n- Same event set, and 'bn admin rebuild' on each still disagrees.\n- With bn sync (pull --rebase, sync.rs:241) the result is 'last pusher wins', not LWW.\n\nRelated order-dependence in the same paths:\n- updated_at_us is set to event.wall_ts_us with no MAX (project.rs field UPDATEs).\n- OR-set remove in apply_event and SQLite labels (project.rs ~470) are add/remove order dependent.\n- project_create ON CONFLICT keeps non-default existing values (project.rs ~300), which depends on whether an update was projected first (ensure_item_exists).\n- apply_phase_transition on Move is order dependent.\n- Incremental projection (incremental.rs:147-300, cursor hash check at :195/:430) can resume mid-stream after a rebase if the hash falls in the 512-byte window. Incremental != full rebuild is possible.\n\nFix directions (design decision needed):\n1. Sort events canonically by (wall_ts, agent, event_hash) before projecting. dag/replay.rs:134 already does this but no projection calls it. Simple. Breaks incremental append-order projection: a late-arriving old event needs a rebuild or per-field compare.\n2. Store LWW metadata per field in SQLite and apply only if the incoming event wins under the same total order. Order-independent and incremental-friendly. More schema work.\n3. Fix .gitattributes precedence so the sorting driver runs. Helps but does not cover rebase or manual file edits, so it is not sufficient alone.\n\nAcceptance: a bones-sim campaign (bn-2fs6) that delivers the same event set in different file orders produces identical projections on every replica, and identical to a full rebuild.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"l","title":"Projection is last-applied-wins in file order; union merge makes replicas diverge","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:4btweYLBJy-w1ZLHmO7yiE5O--jhzHJSc6rvb2XKR6E
1790372066215108	bones-yzou15	itc:v3:AWLJPM5OcyTJJJEAAAAAQdXt13atVUAAAAEzEw		item.link	bn-1ugh	{"link_type":"related_to","target":"bn-t694"}	blake3:b3NeLkDn9FWtdU8Dre2EhSnFh1PO7Eid-HcAROPcL0w
1790372066236839	bones-yzou15	itc:v3:AWLJPM5OcyTJJJEAAAAAQdXt13atVUAAAAEzFA		item.link	bn-1ugh	{"link_type":"related_to","target":"bn-2fs6"}	blake3:ZW4x7SquZXqBhk4dZ7K1yytjKXOR-8mZhDHp8ucF4pg
1790372066256297	bones-yzou15	itc:v3:AWLJPM5OcyTJJJEAAAAAQdXt13atVUAAAAEzFQ		item.comment	bn-24t4	{"body":"Verdict: LwwRegister cycle is LATENT, but a worse bug is REACHABLE. The projection ignores LWW, and union merge reorders lines, so replicas holding the same events diverge even without clock skew. Filed as bn-1ugh with evidence. No canonical order protects any path (dag::topological_order and dag/replay.rs sort are unused by projections)."}	blake3:1pSuJ4wXsnh6_B8WMHJCUnxyb5gUmRHr4GBM1S4LaVQ
