1790373355658887	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsAQ		item.comment	bn-12ta	{"body":"Previous run OOM'd the host: the rle harness looped over symbolic run lengths and cbmc hit 72GB RSS. Harness rewritten to loop only over items and split per encoder. All Kani runs now go through scripts-kani.sh: one harness per systemd scope, MemoryMax=16G, 600s timeout."}	blake3:jSY8zH6JwWIXzH6vwccAm2ZnUQFW5WQZLSChOVeH5Ps
1790373499390946	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsAg		item.comment	bn-2fux	{"body":"Adversarial review: no blockers. Stale docs fixed in the docs commit (ADR-006 amended, notes/plan.md). Known non-blocking items: apply_event casts wall_ts_us as u64 while replay sorts i64, so negative timestamps order differently; identical (wall_ts, agent, hash) with different values is not commutative, but production cannot reach it."}	blake3:rtP9FvdBA25VhZwwEQkrx_3b8iopOIeksAGw7SDZqyM
1790375268868844	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsAw		item.create	bn-52i6	{"description":"Follow-up to bn-t694. LWW now orders by (wall_ts, agent, hash) only. On a machine whose clock lags, a causally later edit can lose to an earlier one. shard.rs next_timestamp is not a hybrid logical clock and does not advance on receive.\n\nFix: when writing an event for an item, set wall_ts_us = max(now, item.updated_at + 1). The writer's projection is its causal past for that item, so causal order then implies wall_ts order for all new writes. Existing logs are unaffected.\n\nAcceptance: unit test: a replica whose clock is 1h behind edits an item last written 'in the future', and its edit wins after merge. ADR-006 amendment updated to say the clamp exists.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"s","title":"Clamp new write wall_ts above the item's latest seen wall_ts"}	blake3:huAOK89NT7x6e6UUxdILj8xbr37uf92pZtYEfhuCmUc
1790375268996607	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsBA		item.create	bn-3is9	{"description":"item_state.rs:215 does 'event.wall_ts_us as u64'. dag/replay.rs and sync/merge.rs sort the signed i64. The parser accepts negative timestamps. A negative wall_ts becomes a huge u64 in LwwRegister, so LWW merge and replay order disagree for it.\n\nFix: reject negative wall_ts_us in the parser/validator, or keep i64 in LwwRegister. Found by the adversarial review of cr-30jx1c.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"xs","title":"apply_event casts wall_ts_us to u64; replay sorts it as i64"}	blake3:wIk5j4nfSqKjmWzkI7HjI8mFZ7wRAgoBisHCLgHKplA
1790375269111684	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsBQ		item.create	bn-1dva	{"description":"just check fails on main at 'cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings' with a newer toolchain:\n- clock/serde.rs:201 read_bit could be const fn\n- crdt/trace.rs:44 and :53, timing.rs:47: '.ok().is_some_and(..)' on Result; use is_ok_and.\nPre-existing, unrelated to the verification work. 'cargo clippy --tests' shows more (config.rs raw strings, parser.rs:1452, model/goal.rs:680).","kind":"task","size":"xs","title":"Fix clippy 1.98 lints that break just check on main"}	blake3:sRNaHrNGBzFDE_iNnWWmb2_sefJJ5s3_r_Pc-I1hQew
1790375269230640	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsBg		item.create	bn-3n8l	{"description":"Running 'seal reviews create' in a workspace copied .crit/reviews/* into .seal/reviews and deleted the tracked .crit/ files and .critignore from the working tree. The deletions are uncommitted in workspace bn-2fux, and the merge status check will flag them. Decide: commit the migration once on main, or restore the files from HEAD. The dcg hook blocks agents from discarding working-tree changes, so a human must restore them.","kind":"task","size":"xs","title":"Decide on seal's .crit to .seal migration deletions in workspaces"}	blake3:F44PswG_OvyArhjfeRGBO5_m2SeC9BnieTdg8fdITDE
