1790377537930694	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsGA		item.create	bn-2gl2	{"description":"Pre-existing, found in review cr-1oltes. A redact that arrives before its target update gives '[redacted]'. A redact that arrives after it leaves the plaintext, because project_redact only rewrites comment bodies (db/project.rs project_redact). A redacted create gives an empty title, a redacted update gives '[redacted]'. Fix: when a redact lands, re-derive the redacted fields: if the target event still owns a field in field_clocks, rewrite that field to '[redacted]'. Add redact to the projection_order property test generator.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"s","title":"Redaction of a title/description update depends on event order"}	blake3:ayN0p6xvoCNhQJV2pcouvNFJqjUY4I9kHCOnj4ineJQ
1790377538060049	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsGQ		item.create	bn-3scg	{"description":"Review note on cr-1oltes. Link members are keyed 'link/<target>/<type>' and resets 'link/<target>*'. A target containing '/' could alias another target's keys. Item IDs are ASCII without '/' today, so the risk is low. Fix: escape or length-prefix the target, or key links in a separate column.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"xs","title":"field_clocks link keys can collide when a target ID contains '/'"}	blake3:mXDVATpKZbSVd2rFU5603mOc1Y5qGnqg_3AT3C53LI8
