1790381463574361	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsIg		item.comment	bn-2fs6	{"body":"Built bones_sim::replica (real replicas, skewed clocks, union/rebase pulls, duplicate-line and dropped-db faults, oracles after every step, shrinking). It found a real bug: incremental apply resumed at a stale cursor after a rebase rewrote the log (skipped events or parse error). Fixed with a schema v4 prefix digest. 1000 seeds pass. With the digest check disabled, seeds 14 and 15 fail (saved as fixtures). With the pre-bn-1ugh projection, almost every seed diverges."}	blake3:GUbwf9-q7FkVkyUUN_fwa8NSubbn4r9j3J0SvGC4j5I
1790381708012098	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsIw		item.move	bn-2fs6	{"state":"done"}	blake3:XS-ky8I6SxZxY2FNpcNWIyybmEO8KHk-zKOnWzclzq0
1790381709642965	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsJA		item.create	bn-2xjb	{"description":"Review cr-9iyreg note 1. rebuild and incremental_apply record the prefix digest by re-reading the log after replay (incremental.rs record_cursor_prefix, called from rebuild.rs and incremental.rs). If git pull --rebase rewrites the log between the replay and the digest read, the digest describes content that was never projected, and later incremental applies skip events. Fix: hash the exact bytes consumed during replay (feed each replayed line into a blake3 hasher) and store that digest. Add a bones-sim fault that rewrites the log between apply and digest, if the driver can reach that window.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"s","title":"Cursor prefix digest is computed after replay, not from the bytes replayed"}	blake3:En3oIEBTajyVLPaJYnw1wCQtOZYLOWar886GL21aTZY
1790381709782654	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsJQ		item.create	bn-3pnu	{"description":"Review cr-9iyreg note 2. MIGRATION_V4_SQL uses ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN, which fails if run twice. If two bn processes migrate at once, the second fails, treats the database as missing, and runs a full rebuild that deletes the file. Once per upgrade, and the projection is derived, so impact is a spurious rebuild. Fix: in migrations::migrate, take BEGIN IMMEDIATE and re-read user_version inside the transaction before applying each migration.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"xs","title":"Concurrent v4 migration can fail and delete the projection"}	blake3:bZeSsDBk4daa5btzHSDRaj-KfYn_T7qFK5QitPpRgOc
1790381709934712	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsJg		item.create	bn-2fn6	{"description":"Review cr-9iyreg note 3. bones-sim covers incremental_apply only. Add bones-core tests: (1) ensure_projection rebuilds when the log is rewritten to the same length and last hash but different earlier content; (2) Projector::project_event records the digest, so the next ensure_projection does not rebuild. Also measure in bones-sim how often the incremental path (not a rebuild) actually runs, so the incremental==rebuild oracle is known not to be trivially satisfied.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"s","title":"Unit tests for the cursor prefix digest in ensure_projection and Projector"}	blake3:RQrykvm0a7IpBdK4OVFkxWerTEmQMxhqElKqfNHo4bI
