1790388526642098	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsPA		item.comment	bn-1veg	{"body":"Tool: Kani (crdt/lww.rs kani_proofs), 3 harnesses, 17-40s each under the 12G cap. Stamp fixed at seed: symbolic ITC stamps hit the memory cap/timeout. Mutations: assert!(false) in transitivity -> FAILED; inverted transitivity assert -> FAILED; event_hash >= to > -> totality FAILED. Reverting the fix (causal step back in compare) is caught by proptest lww_register_associative, not by Kani; recorded in the module doc."}	blake3:rxG8fzqvCViltLAKUquVb6lMO55ESh-iLa6rrDI9JiU
1790388751399297	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsPQ		item.create	bn-2h7c	{"description":"Review note on cr-2dktro (bn-3scg). Nothing stops an older bn (LATEST=4) from writing to a v5 projection. It writes unprefixed link keys that the new binary ignores, so an older link add or removal can win. Fix: in open_projection, when user_version > LATEST_SCHEMA_VERSION, refuse to write or mark the projection dirty. Also add a v4 -> v5 upgrade test that checks the dirty marker and the cleared cursor, like the v3 test.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"xs","title":"Guard projection DBs with a schema newer than the binary"}	blake3:Ijv_1mMp9H7VXf9lGwjh2LXWEMItKd01uIowEZhMzrw
