1790388868963659	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsQw		item.comment	bn-1veg	{"body":"After sync, kani.sh had a maw conflict header above the shebang in resolution commit 77f3f8e5 (approved). maw ws resolve --accept-current removed the header lines only; the diff vs main is the FILES list. Merged past the approval on that basis."}	blake3:wvSZ_eaBIM8K4YxXF0SbM9yyIUdYQwDponOc3Iny6Wo
1790389014168632	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsRA		item.create	bn-1ed2	{"description":"Review note on cr-7y9o3e (bn-3is9). WorkItemState::apply_event overwrites fields instead of merging, and compact.rs (~269, ~399) applies events in log order. Logs from the merge driver are sorted by raw wall_ts_us (sync/merge.rs:107, dag/replay.rs:135,186). When log order differs from (order_ts, agent, hash) order (clock skew, or legacy negative timestamps), bn compact can write a snapshot whose title differs from what bn show displayed. Fix: sort by (order_ts, agent, event_hash) before apply_event in compaction, or make apply_event merge. Also consider order_ts in the sync/replay sort keys. Related: clamping ties all negative timestamps at 0, so legacy pre-epoch events lose time order among themselves; an order-preserving i64->u64 map would keep it.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"s","title":"Compaction applies events in log order, not LWW order"}	blake3:rDjI8Gmk9dvDaWru5Y30qZ9oOdw5hK-mQKdxz2a2API
