1790390144066353	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsSQ		item.create	bn-t37g	{"description":"Review notes on cr-s7sigl (bn-1ed2). Not log-order bugs; WorkItemState and project.rs disagree on these shapes, so bn compact can write a snapshot that differs from bn show:\n1. Create with size/description/parent None does not write the field in item_state; the projection writes NULL. Clock skew (update at t1, create at t2>t1) gives different values. Fix: lww_set None/empty on Create.\n2. Legacy array value for 'labels' update is ignored by item_state; the projection treats it as a group reset.\n3. item_state folds link types into blocks/related buckets and drops other types (bn migrate writes 'relates'); the projection keys each raw link_type. A link removal of 'blocks' also drops a 'blocked_by' link to the same target in the snapshot.\n4. Compact events write description in item_state; the projection writes compact_summary.\n5. Malformed values (non-string title, unparsable kind/urgency) differ.\n6. compacted_from counts duplicate lines, so a replica with a duplicate line gets a different snapshot hash.\n7. Re-running bn compact on an item with a snapshot makes a new snapshot each time.\nSuggested approach: a property test that projects and compacts the same generated events and compares every field.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-274e","size":"s","title":"Snapshot state differs from the projection for some event shapes"}	blake3:O1cpwEEMc-pqu3dyfFkAX6SAjDIWtF7gnpAKonO7QPQ
1790390144095560	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsSg		item.comment	bn-1ed2	{"body":"Review cr-s7sigl LGTM. Follow-up for older snapshot/projection gaps: bn-t37g"}	blake3:cSSQnUwAGW_rLi1YiwLOfZsqp0Pc-_4TjDjMN4bUoLY
