1790393301383867	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsVg		item.move	bn-1dy8	{"state":"done"}	blake3:qOCRI-mhIt6dSWkB5QbufYertIMsIViJ6hJt0bRW9yM
1790394181994779	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsVw		item.comment	bn-226p	{"body":"Spike report (retargeted from ITC to merge kernels; ITC removed in bn-1dy8).\n\nProven by Verus, unbounded, in crates/bones-verified (19 obligations, <1s, ~330MB):\n- bytes_cmp computes byte-lexicographic order; the order is irreflexive, transitive, total.\n- lww_compare computes (wall_ts, agent, event_hash) order + deciding step; the order is a strict total order; key_merge is idempotent, commutative, associative.\n- epoch_phase_join: semilattice laws + least upper bound.\n- min_nonzero / max for created/updated.\nbones-core uses them: LwwRegister::compare, EpochPhaseState::merge, WorkItemState::merge timestamps.\n\nEffort: ~97 exec lines vs ~260 spec/proof lines. Green on the second verification run (one missing precondition). 5 mutations (incl. assert(false) in a lemma) all fail verification. Kani LWW harnesses still pass over the verified compare.\n\nTrusted/unverified glue: str::as_bytes and \"str order = byte order\"; Phase::rank mapping and the joined != self write-back; u8 step -> TieBreakStep match; informal link key_merge -> LwwRegister::merge and \"equal key => equal value\"; OR-Set/G-Set HashSet unions and the deleted register outside the crate; Verus erasure and vstd.\n\nCosts: vstd adds 7 crates to normal builds (incl. verus_syn); vstd is pinned to the exact Verus release; the crate opts out of workspace pedantic clippy; cargo-verus prints nothing on a cache hit (scripts/verus.sh cleans first and requires \"0 errors\").\n\nKani comparison: Kani LWW proofs are bounded (strings <= 2 bytes) at 16-40s each; symbolic ITC trees exceeded the 12G cap. Verus proves the same laws unbounded in under a second.\n\nRecommendation: GO, narrowly. Use Verus for small pure decision kernels that bones-core calls (merge/order functions). Not for SQL, I/O, or std collections. Candidates next: OR-Set membership/tombstone semantics over a Set model, and the snapshot/projection agreement for LWW fields.\n\nNote (review): apply_event's created_at update lets a ts-0 event reset created_at to 0, unlike the verified min_nonzero merge; the projection does the same (MIN incl. 0). Tracked with the snapshot/projection gaps in bn-t37g."}	blake3:Oqk3IwEC9OoeSCHk8r7J8pK0am2rDcN5imRiTyhpsOw
1790394182016378	bones-imvgpj	itc:v3:AWLzPOTyZPOcQAAAAAAAQfb3XrXu4AAAAAEsWA		item.comment	bn-t37g	{"body":"8. apply_event lets a ts-0 event (e.g. clamped negative) reset created_at to 0, while WorkItemState::merge uses the verified min_nonzero; the projection takes MIN including 0. Decide one rule and apply it in all three (review cr-2pcfaz)."}	blake3:nrvKQt_pZqwbr41Vc3adUOcqKqNqI2VOw6Kyy04ic6w
